  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Which of the following statements is true regarding the equilibrium solutions of ${y}^{\u2032}={y}^{2}+6y+9?$",
  "worked_solution": "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{\u2032}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nFirst, we need to find the equilibrium solutions. So, we solve $f(y)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(y) & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}+6y+9 & =0 \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equilibrium solution is $y=-3.$ \n\nNow, we analyze the sign of $f(y)$ using a sign table, as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-3)$ | $(3,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $(y+3)^{2}$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $f(y)$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\nSo, we have that $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nWe can now draw the phase line for this equation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/074ed04c41f20a891678d61a26ae06f1151299110dfd13d2c8b7f6eef3e6e363.png)\n\nFinally, we classify the equilibrium solution:\n\n- $y=-3$ is a node because it is neither a source nor a sink.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$y=-3$ is a node\".",
